## The Corridor Effect Formula

The hall-of-mirrors effect — the signature look of an asscher cut diamond — is not automatic. It requires all five proportion specs working together: when they all fall within ideal ranges, the corridors appear; when any one is out of range, the effect degrades.

Think of it as a formula: **Depth (60–68%) + Table (60–68%) + L/W (1.00–1.05) + Polish (EX/VG) + Symmetry (EX/VG) = Full Corridor Effect.**

If depth is out of range, you get windows or darkness that block the corridors. If the table is out of range, you get a cramped or flat appearance that reduces corridor depth. If the L/W ratio is high, the characteristic square asscher silhouette shifts rectangular.

If polish is poor, the flat step-cut facets scatter light randomly instead of channeling it into clean corridors. If symmetry is poor, the concentric facet alignment breaks down and the corridors become distorted.

A stone that fails even one of these specs can still be sold as "Ideal Cut." A stone that passes all five will produce the full corridor effect regardless of what the vendor calls it.

### Proportion Failure Mode Matrix

This is the diagnostic tool. Use it when evaluating any asscher certificate.

| Spec | Out-of-range value | Visual failure mode | Recovery possible? | What this means |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Depth % | Below 60% | Transparent window in center | No | Stone is permanently windowed — reject |
| Depth % | Above 68% | Dark center, weight penalty | No | Can't fix after cutting — reject |
| Table % | Below 58% | Cramped octagon, reduced entry | No | Light entry restricted — reject |
| Table % | Above 70% | Flat, spread, shallow appearance | No | Crown too low — corridor effect diminished |
| L/W Ratio | Above 1.08 | Rectangular silhouette | No | Buy only if elongated look is intended |
| Polish | Good or below | Surface scatter on step facets | No | Visible in flat step-cut facets — reject |
| Symmetry | Good or below | Misaligned corridors, distorted reflections | No | Structural defect in the cut — reject |

**Verdict:** None of these failures can be fixed after cutting. A stone with a window is windowed forever. A stone with poor symmetry has misaligned corridors forever. This is why checking the certificate before purchase is mandatory, not optional.

