## Lab IGI Asscher — Proportion Standards

Lab grown asscher cut diamonds follow identical proportion standards. D-IF in lab means nothing if the depth is 72% and the stone looks dark. The proportion requirements are the same regardless of origin.

The advantage of lab in proportion terms: IGI, which grades most lab asscher diamonds, does issue cut quality grades for step-cut shapes. An IGI Excellent or Very Good cut grade on a lab asscher is more meaningful than a vendor's "Ideal" on a GIA natural asscher. It is still based on the same proportion data — but it represents an independent assessment, not a vendor's self-certification.

Always verify the underlying numbers even with an IGI cut grade. The summary grade is a shorthand. The actual depth and table percentages are the truth.

